# Fictional EP Tracklist

## 1. Cart Weight Before the First Root

**Story & Context:** During the first weight test, Davi rolls an empty steel plant cart across the hall and records the irregular wheel rhythm as it passes over drain joints in the concrete. He removes the obvious squeaks and keeps only the low impacts. Solveig sustains one open-fifth Hardanger drone over the recording while the main tarraxo kick remains absent for the first sixteen bars.

Elias enters with a baritone-sax subtone slightly below the eventual sub root, creating a tonal floor before the electronics arrive. Mara answers each second drain impact with one hard-damped dulcitone note. When the electronic sub finally appears, it does not increase tempo or density; it simply makes the existing cart rhythm feel heavier.

The track ends with the cart being rolled back in the opposite direction after the drums stop, leaving only sympathetic-string resonance and distant wheel vibration.

