## 3. Drain Channel Holds the Last Beat

**Story & Context:** A narrow drain channel along the packing-hall floor produces a low metallic resonance whenever someone steps across its removable grate. Davi records a single footfall and places it after, rather than on, the final kick of each eight-bar phrase. The late impact becomes the central hook.

Solveig performs short Hardanger phrases that stop just before the delayed footfall, leaving the sympathetic strings exposed. Mara doubles selected grate resonances with deadened dulcitone strikes, while Elias uses only key clicks and air for the first half of the track. When his first fully pitched baritone note arrives, it lands after the groove has already established its low register without him.

In the final minute, the electronic drums disappear. One real footstep crosses the drain channel, the grate rings, Solveig releases the bow, and the EP ends on the sympathetic strings continuing after every obvious source has stopped.

